:LotGroup a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Lot group"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Combination of several lots to conduct comparative assessment of the tenders.

Additional Information:

The comparative assessment may refer to the selection criteria, award and value that apply to several lots.

Pending of discussion with eForms



Member States may provide that, where more than one lot may be awarded to the same tenderer, contracting authorities may award contracts combining several or all lots where they have specified in the contract notice or in the invitation to confirm interest that they reserve the possibility of doing so and indicate the lots or groups of lots that may be combined."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description """Combination of several lots to conduct comparative assessment of the tenders.

Additional Information:

The comparative assessment may refer to the selection criteria, award and value that apply to several lots.

Pending of discussion with eForms



Member States may provide that, where more than one lot may be awarded to the same tenderer, contracting authorities may award contracts combining several or all lots where they have specified in the contract notice or in the invitation to confirm interest that they reserve the possibility of doing so and indicate the lots or groups of lots that may be combined.""" ;
    sh:name "Lot group" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :Lot ;
            sh:name "Sets grouping context for lot" ;
            sh:path :setsGroupingContextForLot ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Sets grouping context for lot" ;
            sh:path :setsGroupingContextForLot ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :AwardCriterion ;
            sh:name "Speficies award criterion" ;
            sh:path :speficiesAwardCriterion ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :MonetaryValue ;
            sh:name "Has estimated value" ;
            sh:path :hasEstimatedValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :SelectionCriterion ;
            sh:name "Speficies selection criteria" ;
            sh:path :speficiesSelectionCriteria ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has estimated value" ;
            sh:path :hasEstimatedValue ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesAwardCriterion> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesAwardCriterion> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesSelectionCriteria> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesSelectionCriteria> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#setsGroupingContextForLot> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#setsGroupingContextForLot> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasEstimatedValue> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasEstimatedValue> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass :LotGroup .

<http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#Address> a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Address"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The particulars of the place where a person or an organisation is located.

WG Approval 28/04/2020

Additional Information:
An "address representation" as conceptually defined by the INSPIRE Address Representation data type: "Representation of an address spatial object for use in external application schemas that need to include the basic, address information in a readable way.".


The representation of Addresses varies widely from one country's postal system to another. Even within countries, there are almost always examples of Addresses that do not conform to the stated national standard. At the time of publication, work is progressing on ISO 19160-1 that defines a method through which different Addresses can be converted from one conceptual model to another.


This specification was heavily based on the INSPIRE Address Representation data type. It is noteworthy that if an Address is provided using the detailed breakdown suggested by the properties for this class, then it will be INSPIRE-conformant. To this very granular set of properties, we add two further properties:

- full address (the complete address as a formatted string)
- addressID (a unique identifier for the address)
The first of these allows publishers to simply provide the complete Address as one string, with or without formatting. This is analogous to vCard's label property.

The addressID is part of the INSPIRE guidelines and provides a hook that can be used to link the Address to an alternative representation, such as vCard or OASIS xAL."""@en ;
    sh:description """The particulars of the place where a person or an organisation is located.

WG Approval 28/04/2020

Additional Information:
An "address representation" as conceptually defined by the INSPIRE Address Representation data type: "Representation of an address spatial object for use in external application schemas that need to include the basic, address information in a readable way.".


The representation of Addresses varies widely from one country's postal system to another. Even within countries, there are almost always examples of Addresses that do not conform to the stated national standard. At the time of publication, work is progressing on ISO 19160-1 that defines a method through which different Addresses can be converted from one conceptual model to another.


This specification was heavily based on the INSPIRE Address Representation data type. It is noteworthy that if an Address is provided using the detailed breakdown suggested by the properties for this class, then it will be INSPIRE-conformant. To this very granular set of properties, we add two further properties:

- full address (the complete address as a formatted string)
- addressID (a unique identifier for the address)
The first of these allows publishers to simply provide the complete Address as one string, with or without formatting. This is analogous to vCard's label property.

The addressID is part of the INSPIRE guidelines and provides a hook that can be used to link the Address to an alternative representation, such as vCard or OASIS xAL.""" ;
    sh:name "Address" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has nuts code" ;
            sh:path :hasNutsCode ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Post code" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#postCode> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Admin unit l1" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#adminUnitL1> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has country code" ;
            sh:path :hasCountryCode ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Address area" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#addressArea> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Admin unit l1" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#adminUnitL1> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Thoroughfare" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#thoroughfare> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Locator name" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#locatorName> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Address area" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#addressArea> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Locator designator" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#locatorDesignator> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Locator designator" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#locatorDesignator> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Full address" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#fullAddress> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Full address" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#fullAddress> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Address i d" ;
            sh:path :addressID ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Locator name" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#locatorName> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Admin unit l2" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#adminUnitL2> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Post name" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#postName> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Admin unit l2" ;
            sh:path <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#adminUnitL2> ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :Identifier ;
            sh:name "Address i d" ;
            sh:path :addressID ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#addressID> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#addressID> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasNutsCode> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasNutsCode> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasCountryCode> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasCountryCode> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#Address> .

:Identifier a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A character string to identify and distinguish uniquely, one instance of an object in an identification scheme from all other objects in the same scheme together with relevant supplementary information."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description "A character string to identify and distinguish uniquely, one instance of an object in an identification scheme from all other objects in the same scheme together with relevant supplementary information." ;
    sh:name "Identifier" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has scheme agency id" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeAgencyId ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has scheme u r i" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeURI ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has scheme i d" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeID ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has scheme data u r i" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeDataURI ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:anyURI ;
            sh:name "Has scheme data u r i" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeDataURI ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has identifier value" ;
            sh:path :hasIdentifierValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has identifier value" ;
            sh:path :hasIdentifierValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has scheme agency name" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeAgencyName ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has scheme name" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeName ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has scheme version i d" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeVersionID ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:anyURI ;
            sh:name "Has scheme u r i" ;
            sh:path :hasSchemeURI ] ;
    sh:targetClass :Identifier .

:ProcurementServiceProvider a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Procurement service provider"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Role of a public or private body which offers ancillary purchasing activities on the market.

Additional information

"Ancillary purchasing activities" means activities consisting in the provision of support to purchasing activities, in particular in the following forms:
(a) technical infrastructure enabling contracting authorities to award public contracts or to conclude framework agreements for works, supplies or services;
(b) advice on the conduct or design of public procurement procedures;
(c) preparation and management of procurement procedures on behalf and for the account of the contracting authority concerned;

Source: Directive 2014/24/EU, Article 2, paragraphs 17 and 15.

This would be equivalent to the concept of 'procuringEntity' in OCDS: 'The entity managing the procurement, which may be different from the buyer who is paying / using the items being procured'.

WG Approval 24/03/2020"""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description """Role of a public or private body which offers ancillary purchasing activities on the market.

Additional information

"Ancillary purchasing activities" means activities consisting in the provision of support to purchasing activities, in particular in the following forms:
(a) technical infrastructure enabling contracting authorities to award public contracts or to conclude framework agreements for works, supplies or services;
(b) advice on the conduct or design of public procurement procedures;
(c) preparation and management of procurement procedures on behalf and for the account of the contracting authority concerned;

Source: Directive 2014/24/EU, Article 2, paragraphs 17 and 15.

This would be equivalent to the concept of 'procuringEntity' in OCDS: 'The entity managing the procurement, which may be different from the buyer who is paying / using the items being procured'.

WG Approval 24/03/2020""" ;
    sh:name "Procurement service provider" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Acts on behalf of" ;
            sh:path :actsOnBehalfOf ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :Buyer ;
            sh:name "Acts on behalf of" ;
            sh:path :actsOnBehalfOf ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#actsOnBehalfOf> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#actsOnBehalfOf> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass :ProcurementServiceProvider .

:Lot a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Lot"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A qualitative, quantitative or strategic subdivision of the goods, services or works to be procured, allowing the award of one or more contracts.

WG approval 12/09/2018"""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description """A qualitative, quantitative or strategic subdivision of the goods, services or works to be procured, allowing the award of one or more contracts.

WG approval 12/09/2018""" ;
    sh:name "Lot" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
            sh:name "Is covered by g p a" ;
            sh:path :isCoveredByGPA ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :SelectionCriterion ;
            sh:name "Speficies selection criterion" ;
            sh:path :speficiesSelectionCriterion ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :LotSpecificTerm ;
            sh:name "Is subject to lot specific term" ;
            sh:path :isSubjectToLotSpecificTerm ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :PlannedProcurementPart ;
            sh:name "Refers to planned part" ;
            sh:path :refersToPlannedPart ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has recurrence description" ;
            sh:path :hasRecurrenceDescription ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Is covered by g p a" ;
            sh:path :isCoveredByGPA ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :ContractSpecificTerm ;
            sh:name "Foresees contract specific term" ;
            sh:path :foreseesContractSpecificTerm ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Is using e u funds" ;
            sh:path :isUsingEUFunds ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :AwardCriterion ;
            sh:name "Speficies award criterion" ;
            sh:path :speficiesAwardCriterion ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Is recurrent" ;
            sh:path :isRecurrent ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
            sh:name "Is recurrent" ;
            sh:path :isRecurrent ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
            sh:name "Is using e u funds" ;
            sh:path :isUsingEUFunds ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Is s m e suitable" ;
            sh:path :isSMESuitable ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has additional information" ;
            sh:path :hasAdditionalInformation ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :TechniqueUsage ;
            sh:name "Uses technique" ;
            sh:path :usesTechnique ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has purpose" ;
            sh:path :hasPurpose ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
            sh:name "Is s m e suitable" ;
            sh:path :isSMESuitable ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :Purpose ;
            sh:name "Has purpose" ;
            sh:path :hasPurpose ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :MonetaryValue ;
            sh:name "Has estimated value" ;
            sh:path :hasEstimatedValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Refers to planned part" ;
            sh:path :refersToPlannedPart ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has recurrence description" ;
            sh:path :hasRecurrenceDescription ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class <http://unknown.domain/for/prefix#Channel> ;
            sh:name "Uses channel" ;
            sh:path :usesChannel ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has estimated value" ;
            sh:path :hasEstimatedValue ],
        <http://myexampleuri.org/data#hasRestatedEstimatedValueShape>,
        <http://myexampleuri.org/data#unitTypeShape> ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasEstimatedValue> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasEstimatedValue> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesSelectionCriterion> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesSelectionCriterion> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#usesTechnique> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#usesTechnique> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesAwardCriterion> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#speficiesAwardCriterion> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasPurpose> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasPurpose> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasReservedProcurement> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasReservedProcurement> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasPerformingStaffQualificationInformation> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasPerformingStaffQualificationInformation> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#foreseesContractSpecificTerm> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#foreseesContractSpecificTerm> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#usesChannel> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#usesChannel> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#refersToPlannedPart> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#refersToPlannedPart> ?this .}" ],
        [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#isSubjectToLotSpecificTerm> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#isSubjectToLotSpecificTerm> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass :Lot .

:Buyer a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Buyer"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A role of an agent that awards a contract and/or purchases items.

Additional information:
In public procurement the role of buyer is carried out by the following types of organisation contracting authority, contracting entity, a defence contractor, an international organisation, or an organisation awarding a contract subsidized by a contracting authority.
In pre-award, the buyer generally awards the contract, however future purchasers may be foreseen.
In post-award the buyer generally refers to the purchaser of items."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description """A role of an agent that awards a contract and/or purchases items.

Additional information:
In public procurement the role of buyer is carried out by the following types of organisation contracting authority, contracting entity, a defence contractor, an international organisation, or an organisation awarding a contract subsidized by a contracting authority.
In pre-award, the buyer generally awards the contract, however future purchasers may be foreseen.
In post-award the buyer generally refers to the purchaser of items.""" ;
    sh:name "Buyer" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Is contracting entity" ;
            sh:path :isContractingEntity ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
            sh:name "Is contracting entity" ;
            sh:path :isContractingEntity ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has buyer profile" ;
            sh:path :hasBuyerProfile ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has activity description" ;
            sh:path :hasActivityDescription ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:class :ProcurementServiceProvider ;
            sh:name "Delegates ancillary activities to" ;
            sh:path :delegatesAncillaryActivitiesTo ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:anyURI ;
            sh:name "Has buyer profile" ;
            sh:path :hasBuyerProfile ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has buyer type description" ;
            sh:path :hasBuyerTypeDescription ],
        <http://myexampleuri.org/data#dependsOnBuyerShape> ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#delegatesAncillaryActivitiesTo> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#delegatesAncillaryActivitiesTo> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass :Buyer .

:MonetaryValue a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:label "Monetary value"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A number of monetary units specified using a given unit of currency.

WG approval 13/04/2021"""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology> ;
    sh:description """A number of monetary units specified using a given unit of currency.

WG approval 13/04/2021""" ;
    sh:name "Monetary value" ;
    sh:property [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has currency code list i d" ;
            sh:path :hasCurrencyCodeListID ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has currency code list agency name" ;
            sh:path :hasCurrencyCodeListAgencyName ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has currency" ;
            sh:path :hasCurrency ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:name "Has amount value" ;
            sh:path :hasAmountValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;
            sh:name "Has amount value" ;
            sh:path :hasAmountValue ],
        [ a sh:PropertyShape ;
            sh:datatype rdfs:Literal ;
            sh:name "Has currency code list agency i d" ;
            sh:path :hasCurrencyCodeListAgencyID ] ;
    sh:sparql [ sh:select "SELECT ?this ?that WHERE { ?this <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasCurrency> ?that . ?that <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/ontology#hasCurrency> ?this .}" ] ;
    sh:targetClass :MonetaryValue .

